       As its return value, mmeemmffdd__ccrreeaattee() returns a new file descriptor  that
       can  be  used to refer to the file.  This file descriptor is opened for
       both reading and writing (OO__RRDDWWRR) and OO__LLAARRGGEEFFIILLEE is set for  the  file
       descriptor.

       With  respect  to  ffoorrkk(2) and eexxeeccvvee(2), the usual semantics apply for
       the file descriptor created by mmeemmffdd__ccrreeaattee().  A copy of the file  de‐
       scriptor  is  inherited  by the child produced by ffoorrkk(2) and refers to
       the same file.  The file descriptor is preserved across eexxeeccvvee(2),  un‐
       less the close‐on‐exec flag has been set.

